| `run_script()` | 215 | `subprocess.run(argv, cwd, env)` | Execute user script | `SUBPROCESS_START` → `SUBPROCESS_EXIT` |
| `write_run()` calls | 203, 250 | `write_run(run, catalog_dir)` twice | Write parquet records before/after subprocess | `PARQUET_WRITE` (2 events) |

**Key detail:** `write_run()` itself is in `catalog.py:16` and calls `pq.write_table(run.to_arrow(), tmp)` at line 22. Both calls in runner.py (lines 203 and 250) must be instrumented separately.

